Declare ioctl() for the socket module on zedBSD.

The socket module sets a socket's blocking mode with ioctl(FIONBIO) when
<sys/ioctl.h> exists and FIONBIO is defined.  FIONBIO reaches it through
other zedBSD headers that carry ioctl request numbers (<uapi/ioctl.h>), but
ioctl() itself is declared only in <sys/ioctl.h>, which the
module includes for a few named systems and otherwise only beside
<netpacket/packet.h>.  zedBSD's build turns the latter off (its packet
sockets do not use struct sockaddr_ll), so zedBSD is named with the systems
that include <sys/ioctl.h> directly.

--- a/Modules/socketmodule.c
+++ b/Modules/socketmodule.c
@@ -203,7 +203,7 @@
 # define USE_GETHOSTBYNAME_LOCK
 #endif
 
-#if defined(__APPLE__) || defined(__CYGWIN__) || defined(__NetBSD__)
+#if defined(__APPLE__) || defined(__CYGWIN__) || defined(__NetBSD__) || defined(__ZEDBSD__)
 #  include <sys/ioctl.h>
 #endif
 
